# T0143 — Security Phase 2: close cross-user access control gaps (IDOR)

Branch: `T0143-authz-reference-scoping` · PROD Task: T0143 (id 156, project 4)

Execution plan for **Phase 2** of the 2026-09 security audit. The umbrella findings record
is [`2026-09-security-audit-remediation.mdc`](2026-09-security-audit-remediation.mdc) and
stays active until Phases 3–7 ship — only this file gets archived at T0143 finish-up.

## Why

The T0112–T0115 ownership migration scoped the project tree, standalone entities, search,
and import/export, but missed **cross-entity reference lookups** and several
**body-supplied parent ids**. Verified by inspection: `src/services/references.ts` and
`src/routes/v1/references.ts` contain zero references to any ownership helper, against 10
in the correctly-scoped `src/routes/v1/search.ts`.

## Work items

### 1. Scope the two unscoped search services (critical)

- `searchEntityReferences` (`src/services/references.ts:103-357`) — accept
  `actorUserId` + `isAdministrator` and apply the right filter per entity type:
  `ownerScope` for ideas/tags, `projectAccessListFilter` for projects,
  `dualScopeListFilter` for tasks/todos/todo lists/image boards, and
  `projectOwnedListFilter` for documents/boards/canvases/wiki nodes. Mirror `search.ts`.
- `searchUserReferences` (`src/services/references.ts:359-417`) — leave the user listing
  intact (mention pickers need it) but see item 5 for the email field.
- `searchTasksForDependency` (`src/services/taskDependencies.ts:289-327`) — thread the
  actor through and apply `dualScopeListFilter`.
- Update both route handlers to resolve `getCurrentUserId` + `userHasAdministrator` first.

### 2. Cross-entity attach IDOR

Each of these confirms the referenced row *exists* but never that the actor may reach it:

| Route | File:line | Fix |
|-------|-----------|-----|
| `POST /projects/:projectId/boards/:boardId/cards` (`entityType=idea`) | `boards.ts:674-679` | `assertCanAccessOwned` |
| Same route (`entityType=todo_list`) | `boards.ts:680-688` | `assertCanAccessDualScoped` — any standalone list from any owner is attachable today |
| `POST /todo-lists/:id/items` | `todoLists.ts:419-431` | `assertCanAccessDualScoped` on the task/todo |
| `POST /projects/:projectId/documents` (`uploadId`) | `documents.ts:110-124` | verify `upload.ownerId` |
| `PATCH /users/me` (`avatarUploadId`) | `users.ts:234-246` | verify `upload.ownerId` |

The todo-list case is the most severe: `GET /todo-lists/:id` hydrates attached entities and
returns title, state, dueDate and priority (`todoLists.ts:210-231`), so the attach doubles
as a read primitive.

### 3. Viewers must not mutate ordering

`PATCH /projects/reorder` (`projects.ts:126-167`) and `PATCH /image-boards/reorder`
(`imageBoards.ts:163-207`) scope by a list filter that includes viewers but never assert
`"write"`. `roleSatisfiesAccess("viewer", "write")` already returns `false` — call it.

### 4. Reject empty-remainder prefix queries

Not a literal empty `q` (Zod enforces `q.min(1)`), but the **type-prefix** path at
`references.ts:55-56`: `?q=T` strips the letter, leaves an empty remainder, and by design
matches everything of that type — `?q=T` all tasks, `?q=I` all ideas, `?q=P` all projects.

Verified safe to close: `client/src/lib/mdReferenceTrigger.ts` returns `null` on an empty
remainder (line 41 for `@`, line 59 for `#`), so `MarkdownReferenceSuggest` never fires
until one character follows the prefix (`#T0`, never `#T`). Zero UX change. Return 400.

### 5. Strip emails from the project user directory

Product decision, revised from an Administrator gate so Managers keep the ability to add
people to their own projects.

- `listProjectDirectoryUsers` (`src/services/projectUsers.ts:507-528`) — return plain
  `UserRef`, drop `email: user.email`.
- `client/src/components/ProjectUsersPanel.tsx` — remove `email` from the candidate type
  (:12), the search haystack (:161) and the ` · email` rendering (:466-467); update the
  placeholder (:442) to drop the email affordance; drop the project owner's email
  (:297-298), which is the same leak class.
- Disambiguation preserved via the existing `referenceId` (`U####`), already rendered and
  searched.
- Residual accepted: Managers can still enumerate display names. Inherent to the picker.

## Testing

Two-user fixture (temporary accounts approved, including Administrator; remove after
verification, never commit credentials). Each route above gets a regression test asserting
user A cannot read or mutate user B's records. Then `npm test`, `npm run lint`, and
`npm run security:scan`.

## Implementation notes (2026-09-18)

Two deviations from the plan as written, both widening scope slightly:

1. **Email stripping went further than the directory.** `GET /projects/:id/users` also
   returned an `email` for every manager, member and viewer, plus the owner — that is the
   most literal instance of "Managers seeing Member email addresses", so `ProjectUserEntry`
   and `ProjectUsersLists.owner` lost the field too, along with the `addUserToProject`
   return. `UserRef.referenceId` still disambiguates.
2. **Reorder needed new helpers rather than a flat `"write"` assert.** `sortOrder` is a
   global column and the nav submits every *accessible* project, so requiring write on all
   of them would have broken reordering for anyone holding a viewer role anywhere. Added
   `projectWriteListFilter` and `dualScopeWriteFilter` to `ownership.ts`; validation still
   spans the readable set, but only write-accessible rows actually move. Viewer-held rows
   keep their position.

Both search services now take a **required** `actor` parameter, so a future caller that
forgets to scope fails to typecheck rather than silently running unscoped.

## Verification

Unit tests (`npm test`, 168 pass): new tests assert the write filters never consult
`project_viewers` / `project_viewer_groups` and are strictly narrower than their read
counterparts, that `searchUserReferences` never touches the users table on an empty query,
and that idea search renders an `owner_id` predicate for non-admins but not for admins.

Live two-user check against DEV with a temporary account (created and deleted, id 8) —
**18/18 passed**. Where the administrator saw 20 tasks / 10 ideas / 4 projects, the second
user saw **0** across all ten entity types plus dependency search; bare prefixes `?q=T|I|P`
returned 400 for both roles; `?q=T0` still returned 200; and neither
`/projects/4/users` nor `/projects/4/users/directory` contained an `email` field.

